    "comment": "Port of the original Kotlin diamondFire.acornPEffect (origin/acorn-0.5.42-SNAPSHOT, app/src/commonMain/resources/assets/) to the three-particles 0.17 schema. Flame emitter timelines are carried over verbatim from the original; alpha envelopes are pre-multiplied into the color keyframes because the instanced renderer has no per-instance alpha (lossless under additive blending). Property-name mapping: acorn forwardDirectionZ -> orientationZ, velocityX -> xVel, forwardVelocity -> forwardVel; acorn's -pi/2-up direction cone becomes a tilt-from-vertical cone around orientationZ = 0. circleInverse easing on the lateral spread became circOut (nearest available). UNIT CONVERSION: the compiled acornui-game.js (origin/kotlin-old docs/) integrates position += forwardVelocity per fixed 0.02 s tick (50 ticks/s), i.e. acorn velocities are px/tick. Scaled by 50 ticks/s and the scene px->m factor (~0.009 m/px, from the original's ~145 px stone ring vs this scene's ~1.3 m ring), the verbatim peak forwardVelocity 2 px/tick is 0.9 m/s. EMISSION PLANE: the original engine rendered this effect in screen space - the emission fan's plane always faced the viewer. In the 3D scene the fan lives in the effect root's local XY plane, so src/fire.ts yaws the root to the camera azimuth each frame; per-particle billboarding only orients the sprites, not the plane the positions spread in. EMBERS: the original's verbatim sparks data (point spawn, 0.29 m sprite via the px conversion, +/-0.9 m/s lateral xVel) read as oversized sparks flung off to the side of the fire; the embers emitter below restores the accepted pre-diamond ember system instead (ellipsoid spawn across the coals, 0.09 m dots, rise with heat and wander, no lateral velocity), with the accepted color/alpha keys pre-multiplied for the instanced renderer.",
